tead", 114.68, 115.06], ["of", 115.06, 115.24], ["washing", 115.24, 115.6], ["around", 115.6, 115.94], ["them,", 115.94, 116.3], ["up", 116.52, 116.66], ["to", 116.66, 116.82], ["65", 116.82, 117.38], ["%", 117.38, 117.78], ["off", 117.78, 118.22], ["right", 118.22, 118.56], ["now.", 118.56, 118.94], ["With", 119.18, 119.38], ["a", 119.38, 119.5], ["90", 119.5, 119.8], ["-day", 119.8, 120.1], ["money", 120.1, 120.42], ["-back", 120.42, 120.7], ["guarantee,", 120.7, 121.22], ["tap", 121.6, 121.76], ["below.", 121.76, 122.18]], "segments": [[0.0, 5.24, "Here's what happens to your airways if you slide two capture cards under your mattress and pillow"], [5.24, 9.64, "and leave them there for four weeks. Slide them in. That's the whole job."], [9.94, 14.36, "The first night, while you sleep, the lure starts drawing dust mites up out of the foam,"], [14.7, 19.46, "the ones building up two inches under your face. That's the plant-derived pheromone lure,"], [19.66, 22.76, "pulling them away from the place you breathe for eight hours a night."], [23.0, 27.02, "By the end of week one, most people find they're not reaching for a tissue the"], [27.02, 32.66, "second they sit up. That's because every mite the lure pulls out stops dropping its 20 pellets"], [32.66, 37.56, "a day of Derpy One where your face sleeps, the allergen that breaks down the junctions"], [37.56, 42.32, "holding your airway lining together. Week two, you stop wondering if you're coming down with"], [42.32, 47.0, "something and that clearer-by-lunch feeling starts showing up at breakfast. That's the"], [47.0, 52.56, "adhesive, locking every mite the lure pulls in, so what it catches comes out of your bed"], [52.56, 58.06, "instead of back into it. The craziest part? You haven't sprayed a thing. You haven't stripped the"], [58.06, 63.26, "bed. You haven't bought a new mattress, but every single night the mattress you sleep on"], [63.26, 68.24, "is giving them up. Week four, by now most people are sleeping through more and waking"], [68.24, 72.68, "up less blocked. Mornings start the way they did years ago, and that background"], [72.68, 78.72, "dread before you even open your eyes is finally gone for you and for whoever shares your bed."], [78.72, 82.38, "How is this possible? Most mite products try to kill them,"], [82.6, 87.18, "but every dead one stays in the bed, carrying the same allergen as a live one."], [87.46, 92.64, "This one pulls them out alive. Dust mites have no eyes. They find each other by scent,"], [92.92, 97.76, "a chemical signal. Capture cards mimic that signal, drawing them up out of the foam,"], [97.96, 102.72, "and the adhesive locks them on. It's lure and trap, the way pest control has"], [102.72, 108.04, "caught things for decades, aimed at the one place nobody had, the inside of a mattress."], [108.46, 113.8, "Because a dead mite can't walk to a card, over 30,000 homes are already pulling them"], [113.8, 120.1, "out of their beds instead of washing around them, up to 65% off right now. With a 90-day"], [120.1, 122.18, "money-back guarantee, tap below."]]}